{
    "pageid": 2734,
    "title": "Creating a mod exe installer guide",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "This guide explains how to create a Windows .exe installer for a CK2 mod , with NSIS ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "An installer will prevent the most frequent causes of a mod not working, reducing the support needed:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "forgetting to remove previous mod version",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "unzipping in wrong folder",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "black flags due to an outdated gfx cache",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "But it may have some drawbacks:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": ".exe files may cause false positive with some antivirus",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ".exe files may be restricted to upload (ex: forum)",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Steps",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Install NSIS-2.46.5-Unicode",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Create a setup.nsi file in same folder as .mod file (see #Sample script )",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Right-click and select Compile NSIS Unicode script",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Rename the .exe with version number, if needed.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Sample script",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "This script is based on When The World Stopped Making Sense setup.nsi script, replacing the mod name by MyMod ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Comments start with ; character."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Note that ;!insertmacro MUI_PAGE_COMPONENTS may be uncommented to display an intermediate page to let user select modules to install. Same behavior can be achieved by installing everything, and letting player select the sub-mods to activate in the launcher."
                }
            ]
        },
